# Storm Herald's returned Auras go "attached to creatures you control" (CR 303.4f): each chosen Aura is offered only the creatures
# it could enchant (the ruling: an Aura that can't be attached to a creature you control can't be returned; CR 303.4i). Animate
# Wall ("Enchant Wall") is offered Bot1's Steel Wall and not Storm Herald, a creature Bot1 controls that it can't enchant. Herald
# has haste: it attacks the turn it is cast (CR 702.10b).
# Turn 1: Lion's Eye Diamond, Mountain, Sol Ring (off the Mountain), Steel Wall (off Sol Ring), then the diamond discards Animate
# Wall and the spare Mountains. Herald is drawn on turn 3 and paid with Mountain and Sol Ring.

[Bot1 Deck]
Lion's Eye Diamond
Mountain
Sol Ring
Steel Wall
Animate Wall
Mountain
Mountain
Storm Herald
Mountain x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Lion's Eye Diamond.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Steel Wall.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Lion's Eye Diamond.Activate(Color: Red)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Storm Herald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Animate Wall)
! Bot1.Choose(Storm Herald)
Bot1.Choose(Steel Wall)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Animate Wall.AttachedTo = Steel Wall
Bot1.Attack(Storm Herald > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 17
